# Delete branch after merge

When a pull request is merged (via GitHub merge, fast-forward of the base, or equivalent), delete its remote head branch right away if it still exists:

```bash
git push origin --delete <head-branch>
git fetch --prune
```

Also delete any other remote branches that are already fully merged into their integration base and have no open PR.

Do not delete `main` (or the repo default branch), and do not delete a branch that is still the base of an open PR or active stacked work.
